WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
[Pointing to a cemetery] They got like a little fence mainly just here.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.200
There's a blue house right here.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.960
At the front end, you'll see the crosses and the cement and everything else.

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.680
I'm going to tell you a little story about that.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.720
The woman and the three kids was there.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.200
Old Man Henry, he was an oyster fisherman.

7
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.900
Well, he passed the hurricane over water out while he was fishing oysters.

8
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.500
He didn't come in.

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.380
The people that were from Cocodrie would go over there.

10
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.440
They stopped, they would look, they'd say, "Let me pick you up and we going to bring you up with us."

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.340
"Oh no," she said.

12
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.560
"I can't go," she said, "when my husband comes in,

13
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.260
if he finds out that I rode with another man to go up," she said, "he's going to beat me.

14
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.320
He's a jealous man."

15
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.180
The woman and the three kids stayed right there and they all drowned.

16
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.240
They picked them up on the other side of Lake Boudreaux over there.

17
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.220
That's where they floated them.

18
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.720
But they could've saved those people's lives.

19
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.200
In those days that's how people were.
